Icon artwork is derived from several upstream sets, each redistributed under
its own licence. The name prefix identifies the source.

  (no prefix)  Phosphor Icons, Copyright (c) 2020 Phosphor Icons
               https://github.com/phosphor-icons/core — MIT License

  lu-          Lucide, Copyright (c) for portions of Lucide are held by
               Cole Bemis 2013-2022 as part of Feather (MIT). All other
               copyright (c) for Lucide are held by Lucide Contributors 2022.
               https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide — ISC License

  fe-          Feather, Copyright (c) 2013-2023 Cole Bemis
               https://github.com/feathericons/feather — MIT License

  tb-          Tabler Icons, Copyright (c) 2020-2024 Paweł Kuna
               https://github.com/tabler/tabler-icons — MIT License

  hi-          Heroicons, Copyright (c) Tailwind Labs, Inc.
               https://github.com/tailwindlabs/heroicons — MIT License

  io-          Iconoir, Copyright (c) 2021 Luca Burgio
               https://github.com/iconoir-icons/iconoir — MIT License

  ms-          Material Symbols (outlined, weight 400),
               Copyright (c) Google LLC
               https://github.com/google/material-design-icons
               Apache License, Version 2.0

  ion-         Ionicons, Copyright (c) 2015-present Ionic
               https://github.com/ionic-team/ionicons — MIT License
               (the MIT terms are the ones reproduced below)

Prefixed artwork is rescaled onto this library's 256-unit grid; the geometry is
otherwise unmodified. The lu-, fe-, tb-, hi- and io- sets are stroked drawings
and are stored as centerline path data, from which every weight is derived. The
ms- and ion- sets are filled artwork with no lighter or heavier variant, so each
ships one weight and every other weight renders that one. Full licence texts,
including the Apache 2.0 text required for the ms- set, are in LICENSES/.

The ion- artwork is extracted from the Ionicons TrueType font as shipped in
@expo/vector-icons, which does not vendor Ionicons' own licence file; the
attribution above is taken from the upstream project.

